Now — the family branch: the ticket says "Scope the vendor-prefix check (`_validateModelEndpoint` prefix branch) and the family-exclusive check to known catalog endpoints". The family check IS already scoped to the three family-exclusive canonical endpoints. But maybe the concern: should the family branch also warn on unknown endpoints? The ticket AC1 only requires the warning for the vendor-prefix case. The "family-exclusive check" is already correctly scoped (passes unknown endpoints). Hmm, but re-reading: "Scope the vendor-prefix check (`_validateModelEndpoint` prefix branch) and the family-exclusive check to **known catalog endpoints** — mirror `_validateWireEndpoint`'s "unknown endpoints pass" rule." — since the family check is already scoped, the work is the prefix branch. I'll keep the family branch as-is (it already mirrors the rule; tests pin it: "a foreign-family id on an UNKNOWN endpoint passes").

