329:/// Wire ⇄ endpoint: a KNOWN endpoint of another API DIALECT is a
330:/// rejection. The catalog carries both layers per record — `kind` is the
331:/// identity/wire label (`zai` routes the openai-completions adapter) and
332:/// `api` is the dialect the endpoint actually speaks — so the comparison
333:/// is dialect-to-dialect: an openai-completions binding on z.ai's
334:/// OpenAI-compatible endpoint passes, an anthropic binding on the same
335:/// endpoint does not. Unknown endpoints pass — there is nothing declared
336:/// to check against.
337:void _validateWireEndpoint({
338:  required ProviderSpec spec,
339:  required String baseUrl,
340:  required String modelId,
341:}) {
342:  for (final endpointSpec in providerCatalog.values) {
343:    if (endpointSpec.defaultBaseUrl.isEmpty) continue;
344:    if (!sameEndpoint(endpointSpec.defaultBaseUrl, baseUrl)) continue;
345:    if (endpointSpec.api == spec.api) return;
346:    throw ConfigException(
347:      'provider/model binding mismatch: model "$modelId" would ride the '
348:      '"${spec.api}" dialect (provider "${spec.name}") against '
349:      '${endpointSpec.name}\'s endpoint $baseUrl — that endpoint speaks '
350:      '"${endpointSpec.api}". Point the binding at the matching endpoint, '
351:      'or declare the explicit `wire:` override only when the endpoint '
352:      'genuinely speaks "${spec.api}"',
353:    );
354:  }
355:}
