329:/// Wire ⇄ endpoint: a KNOWN endpoint of another API DIALECT is a
330:/// rejection. The catalog carries both layers per record — `kind` is the
331:/// identity/wire label (`zai` routes the openai-completions adapter) and
332:/// `api` is the dialect the endpoint actually speaks — so the comparison
333:/// is dialect-to-dialect: an openai-completions binding on z.ai's
334:/// OpenAI-compatible endpoint passes, an anthropic binding on the same
335:/// endpoint does not. Unknown endpoints pass — there is nothing declared
336:/// to check against.
337:void _validateWireEndpoint({
338:  required ProviderSpec spec,
